WebVn TODO
Sequenced work is derived from the design docs in design-docs/ and is a snapshot
as of 2026-08-25 - the dependency edges hold until the work itself changes them,
the size guesses are worth less.

Landed: D (asset manifest), 2026-08-28. Both steps of .scratch/asset-manifest/:
a project declares its own assets in manifest.yaml, and the demo ships the first one.
Its two chains - storage, and asset/label completions in the editor - are now rooted
on what it left behind rather than on it.

Landed: G and the sprite half of .scratch/sprites/, 2026-08-28, as one format
change under formatVersion: 1. All three declarations are keyed maps the script names
ids from; audio carries title/artist and the pause menu shows a now-playing line;
`show` takes an id, so an actor can be on screen more than once. E (AssetResolver) is
unblocked - src/domRenderer/assetPaths.ts is the seam it slots into - and the manifest
shape is settled ahead of the storage chain, which was the point of doing it first.

Landed: .scratch/manifest-editor/, 2026-08-29. manifest.yaml is a second buffer in the
editor, adopted on blur; the ?vn= payload is a two-document stream carrying it; saves are
keyed vn-save-<id> from the manifest rather than the hardcoded "test"; and the asset
loaders report a declared file that is not there instead of hanging on it. That takes the
URL-payload item and its save-keying child below, and the ordering edge between them.
VnEditor has tests and a startEditor harness for the first time, which is the start of T.

Sizes: S = hours, M = a day or two, L = several days.


== READY NOW (nothing blocks these) ==

  A  Find-in-file in the editor, on CodeMirror 5             S
       Three addon imports and a stylesheet. Disposable - the CM6 migration
       deletes it - and there is no reason for it to wait behind anything.
       design-docs/EDITOR.md

  B  Keep the Zod schema in the command registry             S
       registerCommandHandler (Parser.ts:37) keeps the handler and discards the
       schema makeZodCmdHandler closed over. Keeping both is what lets
       completions and docs be derived rather than hand-listed.
       design-docs/EDITOR.md

  C  updateLabels returns ParserError instead of throwing    S
       Label.ts:33 throws a bare uncaught Error. Reachable today with a
       duplicate label; becomes routine once includes exist.
       design-docs/SCRIPT_INCLUDES.md

  E  AssetResolver indirection                               M
       The seven call sites that concatenated asset paths are now four calls
       into src/domRenderer/assetPaths.ts, which resolves an id to a path.
       One interface behind that makes the storage backend swappable.
       Two implementations, one per entry point and both permanent: OPFS for
       the editor, URLs for the player. The player does not import to read.
       design-docs/PROJECT_STORAGE.md

  F  Parser benchmark at 1k/10k/50k commands, written down   S
       Spike. Settles whether YAML parse time is worth designing around, and
       says which of parse / updateLabels / time-to-first-stop dominates.

  H  Measure the tree-shaken zip.js reader bundle            S
       Spike. Shipped bundles gzip to ~79-85KB but include mime tables,
       encryption and wasm codecs. Decides zip.js against unzipit + client-zip.
       design-docs/PROJECT_STORAGE.md

  T  Behavioural editor tests                                M
       Started: test/helpers/vnHarness.ts's startEditor mounts one, and
       test/browser/VnEditor.test.ts covers adopt-on-blur. Still nothing on the
       jump modes, the gutter markers or loadScript. Written as "this script
       produces these errors and this player state" they survive the CM6
       rewrite; written against .CodeMirror-* classes they do not.


== STORAGE ==  design-docs/PROJECT_STORAGE.md

  E -> OPFS project store                                L
             author-chosen id directories, tmp-then-move writes,
             enumeration as truth
             |
             +-> project rename: copy + delete, editor.yaml     M
             |     pendingRename marker, quota precheck, overwrite dialog.
             |     No engine implements directory move; the recursive walk
             |     is shared with zip import/export.
             +-> project library UI                          M
             |     |     Hosts the first-run story: an empty picker is the
             |     |     worst introduction to an authoring tool, so the
             |     |     "load the demo" button below lives here.
             |     +-> persist() + estimate() + export nag    S
             +-> navigator.locks for two-tab autosave         S
             +-> linked-folder layer  (after zip import/export)     M
             |     |     showDirectoryPicker() is the only way to write a
             |     |     directory tree out of a browser, so this is the
             |     |     folder export, not a convenience - but Chromium
             |     |     only, which is why the archive ships first.
             |     +-> IndexedDB handle store
             +-> import: shared back half + size/entry caps    M
             |     |     SourceLoader in front, so a new ingestion path
             |     |     is a loader and not a subsystem. Validate the
             |     |     manifest, write the tree, raise the collision
             |     |     dialog. All four paths share this.
             |     +-> publish: static folder                       M
             |     |     The demo is the first one, laid out in dist/
             |     |     in the OPFS shape. URL import reads it back.
             |     +-> URL import + "load the demo" button          M
             |     |     Same-origin first, so CORS is not a variable
             |     |     in the first attempt. The manifest is the file
             |     |     index; a partial fetch fails the whole import.
             |     +-> zip import/export  (needs H)                 M
             |     |     <project-id>.webvn.zip, manifest at the archive
             |     |     root. Sniffs PK\x03\x04 not the extension, strips
             |     |     a single wrapping dir, identity from the manifest
             |     |     id. Export must NOT ship ahead of this.
             |     +-> single-file HTML export
             |     +-> downscale on import (optional)
             +-> content addressing (optional, cheaper now than later)

  E -> object URL lifetime test (cloneNode against a revoked blob URL)


== EDITOR ==  design-docs/EDITOR.md

  Manifest editing landed 2026-08-29: two buffers on one CodeMirror instance, a tab bar
  over them, adopt-on-blur. The tab bar is what grows into the file switcher below - CM6
  supplies the buffer model and no UI for choosing between buffers.

  T -> CM6 migration                                         L
         +-> autocompletion  (needs B)                              M
         |     +-> documentation popup                        S
         +-> Enter / list continuation                        S
         +-> inline diagnostics via @codemirror/lint (optional)
         +-> editor multi-buffer  (shared with includes)

  A stands alone and is deleted by the migration.


== SCRIPT INCLUDES ==  design-docs/SCRIPT_INCLUDES.md

  C + SourceLocation gains a file + OPFS project store
         +-> SourceLoader, node-level flattening, cycle detection    M
               +-> export flattening
  CM6 migration + SourceLocation
         +-> editor multi-buffer, file switcher, per-buffer markers  L


== THE EDGES THAT DECIDE ORDERING ==

  CM6 before editor multi-buffer, or multi-buffer gets built twice.
  OPFS store before the includes resolver, or SourceLoader gets written twice.

  D -> E -> OPFS store -> library UI + zip export is what turns this into a tool
  someone other than its author can use. Everything in the editor chain is
  quality of life on top of an authoring loop that does not exist yet.

  F and H are pure measurement. Each retires an open question rather than
  building anything.


== UNSEQUENCED ==

  Nothing below came out of the design docs; no dependencies claimed.

  NVL mode

  Note (text message) system
    TextBoxType has only ADV, with a "todo maybe note at some point" comment.

  Text node parsing (colors, text speed)
    TextNode already carries color and characterDelay, but Say hardcodes
    characterDelay: 20 and takes the colour from the actor. Nothing parses
    per-node markup.

  Sprites
    Sprite flipping
    Position presets   - ShowCommandSchema accepts `position` and apply()
                         ignores it entirely

  Decision showIf
    Show/hide individual decision options based on variables.

  Arbitrary transformation matrix for backgrounds
    Currently pan and scale via four-number viewboxes.

  Rewrite the audio renderer against WebAudioContext
    To close the Chrome gapless-looping problem.
